    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt package to satisfy the specification:\n\n1. **varint.py**: Fixed `decode_uvarint` to properly decode multi-byte LEB128 varints (was broken, only reading single byte and masking high bit).\n\n2. **header.py**: Changed count field encoding from big-endian (`>I`) to little-endian (`<I`) u32, matching the actual sample format.\n\n3. **crc.py**: \n   - Added final XOR (`^ 0xFFFFFFFF`) to `compute_crc` to produce standard CRC-32 (was missing, making it a non-standard variant).\n   - Added `IncrementalCRC` class for streaming CRC computation without loading entire data into memory.\n   - Changed `unpack_crc` to raise `WFormatError(\"truncated\")` instead of `ValueError`.\n\n4. **codec.py**: \n   - Updated `unpack` to verify CRC checksum before parsing records.\n   - Updated `verify` to catch both `WFormatError` and generic exceptions, never raising.\n   - Proper structure validation with appropriate error kinds.\n\n5. **stream.py**: Complete rewrite for true streaming:\n   - Uses only fixed-size ",
